{%- doc -%}
  Outputs "true" when a product should stay out of product lists: collections, search,
  predictive search and recommendations. Used for products that only exist to be added by
  the theme itself, such as gift wrap.

  A product is hidden with Shopify's own metafield seo.hidden set to 1. That metafield
  also keeps it out of Shopify's search and the sitemap. It works with and without a
  metafield definition in the admin.

  @param {object} product - The product to check

  @example
  {% capture hidden %}{% render 'product-hidden', product: product %}{% endcapture %}
  {% if hidden == 'true' %}{% continue %}{% endif %}
{%- enddoc -%}

{%- liquid
  assign seo_hidden = product.metafields.seo.hidden
  if seo_hidden.value == 1 or seo_hidden == 1 or seo_hidden.value == '1' or seo_hidden == '1'
    echo 'true'
  endif
-%}
